---
/**
 * Pure CSS scroll-driven story. No JavaScript.
 * Falls back to static stacked beats without animation-timeline / reduced motion.
 */
---

<section class="scroll-story section-gap" aria-labelledby="story-title">
  <h2 id="story-title">How a tag changes without changing</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    The label in your workflow can stay put while the commit underneath swaps. Refledger records the
    swap.
  </p>

  <div class="scroll-story-track">
    <div class="scroll-story-sticky">
      <article class="scroll-beat">
        <h3>1. Your workflow pins a label</h3>
        <p class="mono">uses: some-org/action@v1.0.0</p>
        <p>Points at commit <span class="mono">a1b2c3d</span>.</p>
        <ul>
          <li class="mono">action.yml</li>
          <li class="mono">dist/index.js</li>
          <li class="mono">README.md</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="scroll-story-sticky">
      <article class="scroll-beat">
        <h3>2. The label stays. The commit does not.</h3>
        <p class="mono">uses: some-org/action@v1.0.0</p>
        <p>
          Still the same string in your repo. Underneath, the tip now points at
          <span class="mono">e4f5a6b</span>. The file list changed. Nothing in your workflow file
          moved.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li class="mono">action.yml</li>
          <li class="mono">dist/index.js <em>(changed)</em></li>
          <li class="mono">payload.bin <em>(added)</em></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
    <div class="scroll-story-sticky">
      <article class="scroll-beat">
        <h3>3. The wall jogs. A ledger entry appears.</h3>
        <p>
          Seq, time window, from and to. Facts you can verify. No verdict about intent.
        </p>
        <p class="mono">
          seq 57 · floating major · content change · ahead<br />
          from 1129829 → to 13465d0
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
